    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0730" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg636"/>

                <head>No. 392.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stallo to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-06-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 28, 1887</date>. (Received July
                        ll.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 137.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The difficulties which prevented the
                    meeting of the representatives of the several states at Rome at the time
                    appointed by the last conference<anchor n="*" xml:id="d392-f1"/> have not yet
                    been removed; and I was informed a few days <pb facs="0731" n="637"
                        xml:id="pg637"/> ago, upon inquiry at the foreign office, that the meeting
                    may not take place for some months to come. Whenever it takes place I shall, of
                    course, attend it, and shall deposit the protocol in question and do whatever
                    else is necessary to give full effect to the intentions of the President and
                    Senate.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Stallo</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
